      "start": 170.92,
      "end": 173.56,
      "text": "n gets the value zero you're going to print n."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.74,
      "end": 177.44,
      "text": "Then you're going to go back to the top"
    },
    {
      "start": 177.44,
      "end": 179.92,
      "text": "n gets the value one then you're going to go"
    },
    {
      "start": 179.92,
      "end": 182.92,
      "text": "execute whatever's inside so you're going to print one."
    },
    {
      "start": 184.36,
      "end": 185.62,
      "text": "Then you're going to increment that"
    },
    {
      "start": 185.62,
      "end": 187.04,
      "text": "to the next value in the sequence"
    },
    {
      "start": 187.04,
      "end": 189.26,
      "text": "you're going to print out two and so on."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.48,
      "end": 195.84,
      "text": "So this is the general look of a for loop."
    },
    {
      "start": 196.04,
      "end": 199.8,
      "text": "So we have for some loop variable again"
    },
    {
      "start": 199.8,
      "end": 203.84,
      "text": "can be named whatever you want in range some number"
    },
    {
      "start": 205.02,
      "end": 208.76,
      "text": "do a bunch of stuff and again"
    },
    {
      "start": 208.76,
      "end": 210.72,
      "text": "these are part of this for loop code block"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.72,
      "end": 212.98,
      "text": "so you should indent them to tell Python"
    },
    {
      "start": 212.98,
      "end": 214.58,
      "text": "that these are the things that you should do."
    },
    {
      "start": 216.16,
      "end": 218.22,
      "text": "So when you're using range some number"
    },
    {
      "start": 218.22,
      "end": 222.84,
      "text": "you start out with variable getting the value zero."
    },
    {
      "start": 225.78,
      "end": 228.12,
      "text": "With variable having value zero"
    },
    {
      "start": 228.12,
      "end": 230.06,
      "text": "you're going to execute all of these expressions."
    },
    {
      "start": 231.58,
      "end": 234.28,
      "text": "After all the expressions in the code block are done"
    },
    {
      "start": 234.28,
      "end": 238.46,
      "text": "you're going to go on to the next value so one."
    },
    {
      "start": 239.48,
      "end": 241.62,
      "text": "You're going to execute all these expressions"
    },
    {
      "start": 241.62,
      "end": 246.46,
      "text": "with variable being value one and then so on and so on"
    },
    {
      "start": 246.46,
      "end": 249.26,
      "text": "until you go to sum num minus one."
    },
    {
      "start": 255.18,
      "end": 258.68,
      "text": "So using range in that way is a little bit constraining"
    },
    {
      "start": 259.4,
      "end": 261.98,
      "text": "because you're always going to get values starting from zero"
    },
    {
      "start": 261.98,
      "end": 264.64,
      "text": "and ending at sum num minus one."
    },
    {
      "start": 265.24,
      "end": 267.16,
      "text": "Whatever's in the parentheses in range."
    },
    {
      "start": 267.98,
      "end": 269.38,
      "text": "Sometimes you might want to write programs"
    },
    {
      "start": 269.38,
      "end": 271.2,
      "text": "that maybe start at a custom value."
    },
    {
      "start": 271.48,
      "end": 273.1,
      "text": "Don't start at zero maybe they start at five"
    },
    {
      "start": 273.68,
      "end": 275.02,
      "text": "maybe it started minus ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 276.36,
      "end": 278.02,
      "text": "And sometimes you might want to write programs"
    },
    {
      "start": 278.02,
      "end": 280.3,
      "text": "that don't go with don't increment"
    },
    {
      "start": 280.3,
      "end": 283.0,
      "text": "the numbers by one but maybe skip every other number"
    },
    {
      "start": 283.0,
      "end": 285.42,
      "text": "or go every two numbers every three numbers and so on."
    },
    {
      "start": 285.94,
      "end": 289.68,
      "text": "So you can customize range to your needs."
    },
    {
      "start": 291.02,
      "end": 293.44,
      "text": "The one thing you do need to give it is the stop."
    },
    {
      "start": 294.04,
      "end": 296.12,
      "text": "So if you give it only one value in the parentheses"
    },
    {
      "start": 296.12,
      "end": 297.8,
      "text": "that stands for stop."
    },
    {
      "start": 298.7,
      "end": 300.0,
      "text": "And by default start is going to have the value zero"
    }
  ],
